Exports cds alignments, perform clean-up with Translator X + Gblocks, and use the AU test implemented in CONSEL to reject gene trees violating species phylogenies.
Label foreground clades and background clades to prepare for relax tests.

Set paths to 3rd-party software in config.php
ret_DNA.fasta.gz contains all aligned CDS sequences prior to any trimming, useful for obtaining the AA positions after alignment
ret_improved_cleanDNA.fasta.gz contains all aligned and cleaned sequences, which should be used for phylogenies and downstream analysis.

Automatic cleaning is necessary to minimize false positive results in selection analyses, but this process may be over-aggressive and thus is conservative.
For key candidate genes, it is recommended to grep the gene from ret_DNA.fasta.gz and perform manual cleaning.
